{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-15225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/assets/6c70d5f15424c4d7d67a3998a785a214e46e8dfa47b83839fd99a574b2f756cf.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$, which is defined on $[-1,6]$, is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(4,0)$ with radius $1.$ Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[0,5].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,3].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [3,5].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5-0}\\cdot (3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7b92142725c210573acf7b23c225b00b3462387b68f80564e2919b6535ab704"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+\\frac{\\pi }{10}"] ["math" "1-\\frac{\\pi }{5}"] ["math" "3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "5+\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-30752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the average value of $h(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ on the interval $[\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-30752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}h(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }{(\\frac{1}{2})(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }(-1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-30752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7b92142725c210573acf7b23c225b00b3462387b68f80564e2919b6535ab704"} {"question" "q-30752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-30752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{\\pi }"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{\\pi }"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-30752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{\\pi }"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-74070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=3-2x$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-74070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}(3-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 1 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(3x-{x}^{2})|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(3c-{c}^{2})-(0)] \\\\ 1 & =3-c \\\\ -2 & =-c \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-74070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7b92142725c210573acf7b23c225b00b3462387b68f80564e2919b6535ab704"} {"question" "q-74070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-74070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-74070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-316302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)={cos}^{8}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ on the interval $[0,\\pi ].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-316302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{8}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this integral using a substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{8}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{8}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{{u}^{9}}{9})|}_{1}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9\\pi }[(-1)^{9}-{1}^{9}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-316302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7b92142725c210573acf7b23c225b00b3462387b68f80564e2919b6535ab704"} {"question" "q-316302" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-316302" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{9\\pi}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-344702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/assets/8ddd8493662174e0ddaf9bdd63b0ec382f6bb25c9079f1a339b71400b8cf3860.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-6,6],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $15$, $60$ and $9,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-6,6].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-344702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-15+60-9=36.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-(-6)}\\cdot (36) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{12} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-344702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7b92142725c210573acf7b23c225b00b3462387b68f80564e2919b6535ab704"} {"question" "q-344702" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"} {"question" "q-344702" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a3e7bedc305c5ca9d507086198e6ed35852e5dcbf441f714affeac3c260d8ae"}] "usage" {"q-30752" []} "basis" 1982 "retractions" [[17592186101281 :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nWhat is the average value of $h(x) = \\sin 2x$ on the interval $[\\frac{π}{4}, \\frac{π}{2}]$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186099317 17592186099318 17592186099319 17592186099320 17592186099321] "immutable_fields" [[17592186099316 :answer-field/correct] [17592186099316 :answer-field/id] [17592186099316 :answer-field/key] [17592186099316 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
